(nature, such as can be performed by the pupils themselves with a) Tj T*
(moderate expenditure of ingenuity and money. The experience of the) Tj T*
(writer has been that for the average boy or girl who wishes to get) Tj T*
(a good general knowledge of the subject, but does not propose to) Tj T*
(become a specialist in botany, the best results are often obtained) Tj T*
(by the use of the simplest and most familiar appliances, as in) Tj T*
(this way attention is not distracted from the experiment itself to) Tj T*
(the unfamiliar apparatus for making it. In saying this, it is not) Tj T*
(meant to underrate the value of a complete laboratory equipment,) Tj T*
(but merely to emphasize the fact that the lack of it, while a) Tj T*
(disadvantage, need not be an insuperable bar to the successful) Tj T*
(teaching of botany. It is, of course, taken for granted that in) Tj T*
(schools provided with a suitable laboratory outfit, teachers will be) Tj T*
(prepared to supplement or to replace the exercises here outlined with) Tj T*
(such others as in their judgment the subject may demand. There are as) Tj T*
(many ideals in teaching as there are teachers, and the most that a) Tj T*
(textbook can do is to present a working model which every teacher is) Tj T*
(free to modify in accordance with his or her own method.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The writer takes pleasure in acknowledging here the many obligations) Tj T*
