(physical basis of all life. Cells are commonly more or less rounded) Tj T*
(in shape, though they take different forms according to the purpose) Tj T*
(they serve. Sometimes, as in the fibers of cotton and the down of) Tj T*
(young leaves, they are long and hairlike; when closely packed, they) Tj T*
(often become angular by pressure, like those shown in Figs. 10, 11.) Tj T*
(The cells composing the thick body of the bean are for the most) Tj T*
(part starch and other substances stored up for food, which render) Tj T*
(observation difficult. It will, therefore, be better to choose for a) Tj T*
