(  number of dry seeds of different kinds?squash, bean, castor bean,) Tj T*
(  quince, etc.?in warm water and notice whether any bubbles of air) Tj T*
(  form on them and at what point. Examine with a lens and see if this) Tj T*
(  point differs in any way from the rest of the seed cover. Does it) Tj T*
(  correspond with the point from which water exuded in the soaked) Tj T*
(  seeds? Could hard seeds like the squash, castor bean, buckeye, and) Tj T*
(  Brazil nut get water readily without an opening somewhere in the) Tj T*
(  coat?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  EXPERIMENT 13. TO FIND OUT WHETHER WATER IS ABSORBED THROUGH THE) Tj T*
(  SEED COATS.?Place in moist sand or sawdust two rows of beans as) Tj T*
(  nearly as possible of the same size and weight, with the eye) Tj T*
(  pressed down to the substratum in one row and turned up in the) Tj T*
(  other, so that no moisture can enter through it. In the same way) Tj T*
(  arrange two rows of castor beans with the little end down in one) Tj T*
(  row and uppermost in the other. In the last set carefully break) Tj T*
(  away the spongy mass near the tip, without injuring the parts about) Tj T*
(  it. Watch and see in which rows water is absorbed most readily.) Tj T*
(  What change takes place in the spongy masses at the tips of those) Tj T*
(  castor beans on which they were left?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 13.?Effect of the expansion of seeds due to) Tj T*
(absorption of water.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  EXPERIMENT 14. IS THE RATE OF GERMINATION AFFECTED BY THE PRESENCE) Tj T*
(  OR ABSENCE OF OPENINGS??Seal up with wax or paraffin all the) Tj T*
(  openings of a number of air-dry peas or beans, and leave an equal) Tj T*
(  number of the same size and weight untreated. Be careful that the) Tj T*
(  sealing is absolutely water-tight, since otherwise the experiment) Tj T*
(  will be worthless. Plant both sets and keep under like conditions) Tj T*
(  of soil, temperature, and moisture. Do you see any difference in) Tj T*
(  the rate of germination of the two sets?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
