(is characteristic of the great natural division of Gymnosperms, or) Tj T*
(naked-seeded plants, of which we have had an example in the pine.) Tj T*
(They are the most primitive type of living seed-bearing plants.) Tj T*
(Though they are not so abundant now as in past ages, numbering only) Tj T*
(about four hundred known species, they present many diversities of) Tj T*
(form, which seem to ally them on the one hand with the lower, or) Tj T*
(spore-bearing plants \(ferns, mosses, etc.\), and on the other hand) Tj T*
(with the Angiosperms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
