(=19. Agencies of dispersal.=?The means at nature?s disposal for this) Tj T*
(purpose, as shown by the experiments just made, are four; namely,) Tj T*
(wind, water, the explosion of capsules due to the withdrawal of) Tj T*
(water, and the agency of animals, including man. The first three) Tj T*
(are purely mechanical. The last, animal agency, is either voluntary) Tj T*
(or involuntary, according as it is conscious and intentional, or) Tj T*
(accidental merely. Man, of course, is the only consciously voluntary) Tj T*
(agent. Of the four agencies named, animals and wind are the most) Tj T*
(effective, and the greater number of adaptations observed will be) Tj T*
(found to have reference to these.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 37.?Good quality of clover seed.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 38.?Inferior quality of clover seed mixed with) Tj T*
(?screenings.?]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 39.?Dodder on red clover, showing how the seeds) Tj T*
(get mixed.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=20. Involuntary dispersal.=?The lower animals may be voluntary) Tj T*
(agents in a way, though not designedly so, as when a squirrel buries) Tj T*
(nuts for his own use and then forgets the location of his hoard and) Tj T*
(leaves them to germinate; or when a jaybird flies off with a pecan) Tj T*
(in his bill, intending to crack and eat it, but accidentally lets) Tj T*
(it fall where it will sprout and take root. Both man and the lower) Tj T*
(animals are not only involuntary, but often unwilling agents of) Tj T*
(dispersal. Some of the most troublesome weeds of civilization have) Tj T*
(been unwittingly distributed by man as he journeyed from place to) Tj T*
(place, carrying, along with the seed for planting his crops, the) Tj T*
(various weed seeds, or ?screenings,? as these mixtures are called) Tj T*
(by dealers, with which they have been adulterated either through) Tj T*
(carelessness and ignorance, or from unavoidable causes. The neglected) Tj T*
(animals, also, that are allowed by short-sighted farmers to wander) Tj T*
(about with their hair full of cockleburs and other adhesive weed) Tj T*
(pests, are no doubt very unwilling carriers of those disagreeable) Tj T*
(burdens.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=21. Tempting the appetite.=?This is the most important adaptation) Tj T*
(to dispersal by animals. Have you ever asked yourself how it could) Tj T*
(profit a plant to tempt birds and beasts to devour its fruit, as so) Tj T*
(many of the bright berries we find in the autumn woods seem to do? To) Tj T*
(answer this question, examine the edible fruits of your neighborhood) Tj T*
(and you will find that almost without exception the seeds are hard) Tj T*
