(          Field Work) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  The subjects treated in the foregoing chapter are, in general,) Tj T*
(  better suited to laboratory than to field work. There are some) Tj T*
(  details, however, which can be observed to advantage out of doors.) Tj T*
(  Many of the seeds found in your walks will show peculiarities of) Tj T*
(  shape and external markings and color that will invite observation.) Tj T*
(  Examine also the contents of different kinds you may meet with, as) Tj T*
(  to the presence or absence of endosperm and the arrangement and) Tj T*
(  development of the embryo. Note: \(1\) whether, as a general thing,) Tj T*
(  there is any difference in size and weight and amount of nourishing) Tj T*
(  matter in the two kinds; \(2\) the greater variety in the shape and) Tj T*
(  arrangement of the cotyledons in the albuminous kind, and in the) Tj T*
(  arrangement of the embryo; \(3\) the differences in the development) Tj T*
(  of the plumule in the two kinds,?and give a reason for the facts) Tj T*
(  observed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  Among the different seeds you may find, look for adaptations for) Tj T*
(  dispersal, and decide to what particular method each is suited.) Tj T*
(  Study the agencies by which various kinds may get covered with) Tj T*
(  soil. If the common stork?s-bill \(_Erodium cicutarium_\) grows in) Tj T*
(  your neighborhood, its seeds will well repay a little study, and if) Tj T*
(  there is a field of peanuts within reach, do not fail to pay it a) Tj T*
(  visit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER II. GERMINATION AND GROWTH) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(          I. PROCESSES ACCOMPANYING GERMINATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  MATERIAL.?A pint or two of corn, peas, beans, or any quickly) Tj T*
(  germinating seed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  APPLIANCES.?Matches; wood splinters; gas jet or alcohol lamp; test) Tj T*
(  tubes; a small quantity of mercuric oxide; a thermometer; a couple) Tj T*
(  of two-quart preserve jars, and a smaller wide-mouthed bottle that) Tj T*
(  can be put into one of them; some limewater; a glass tube \(the) Tj T*
(  straws used by druggists for soft drinks will answer\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=26. Preliminary exercises.=?Before taking up the study of) Tj T*
(germinating seeds, it is important to learn from what sources the) Tj T*
(organic substances used by the growing plant are derived, and some of) Tj T*
(the processes that accompany growth and development.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  EXPERIMENT 21. TO SHOW THE CHANGES THAT ACCOMPANY OXIDATION.?Strike) Tj T*
(  a match and let it burn out. Examine the burnt portion remaining) Tj T*
(  in your hand; what changes do you notice? These changes have been) Tj T*
(  caused by the union of some substance in the match with something) Tj T*
(  outside of it, in the act of burning; let us see if we can find out) Tj T*
ET
endstream
