<< /Length 3420 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(  what this outside substance is.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  EXPERIMENT 22. TO SHOW THE ACTIVE AGENT IN OXIDATION.?Heat some) Tj T*
(  mercuric oxide in a test tube over the flame of a burner. The) Tj T*
(  heat will cause the oxygen to separate from the mercury, and in a) Tj T*
(  short time the tube will be filled with the gas. Extinguish the) Tj T*
(  flame from a lighted splinter and thrust the glowing end into the) Tj T*
(  tube; what happens? The oxygen unites with something in the wood) Tj T*
(  and causes it to burn just as the match did. Compare your burnt) Tj T*
(  splinter with the burnt end of the match; what resemblance do you) Tj T*
(  notice between them?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  EXPERIMENT 23. TO SHOW THAT CARBON DIOXIDE IS A PRODUCT OF) Tj T*
(  OXIDATION.?Your experiment with the match showed that ignition) Tj T*
(  is accompanied by heat, and if active enough, by light, and also) Tj T*
(  that it left behind a solid substance in the form of charcoal. But) Tj T*
(  how about the part that united with the oxygen to produce these) Tj T*
(  results? Let us see what became of it. Hold a lighted candle) Tj T*
(  under the open end of a test tube, or under the mouth of a small) Tj T*
(  glass jar. Does any vapor collect on the inside? After two or) Tj T*
(  three minutes quickly invert the jar or the tube, and thrust in a) Tj T*
(  lighted match: what happens? Can the substance now in the jar be) Tj T*
(  ordinary air? Why not? \(Exps. 21, 22.\) Pour in a small quantity of) Tj T*
(  limewater, holding your hand over the mouth of the tube to prevent) Tj T*
(  the air from getting in; the gas inside, being heavier than air,) Tj T*
(  will not escape immediately unless agitated. What change do you) Tj T*
(  notice in the limewater?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  It has been proved by experiment that the kind of gas formed by) Tj T*
(  the burning candle has the property of turning limewater milky;) Tj T*
(  hence, whenever you see this effect produced in limewater, you may) Tj T*
(  conclude that this gas, known as _carbon dioxide_, is present;) Tj T*
(  and conversely, the presence of carbon dioxide, especially if) Tj T*
(  accompanied by some of the other effects observed, as the giving) Tj T*
(  out of heat and moisture, may be taken as evidence that some) Tj T*
(  process similar to that going on in the burning candle is, or has) Tj T*
