(=40. Organs of vegetation.=?The three parts, root, stem, and leaf,) Tj T*
(are called organs of vegetation in contradistinction to the flower) Tj T*
(and fruit, which constitute the organs of reproduction. The former) Tj T*
(serve to maintain the plant?s individual existence, the latter to) Tj T*
(produce seed for the propagation of the species, so we find that the) Tj T*
(seed is both the beginning and the end of vegetable life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
