(=51. Geotropism.=?The general tendency of the growing axes of) Tj T*
(plants to take an upward and downward course as shown in Exp.) Tj T*
(37?in other words, to point to and from the center of the earth?is) Tj T*
(called _geotropism_. It is _positive_ when the growing organs point) Tj T*
(downward, as most primary roots do; _negative_ when they point) Tj T*
(upward, as in most primary stems; and _transverse_, or _lateral_,) Tj T*
(when they extend horizontally, as is the case with most secondary) Tj T*
(roots and branches.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=52. Gravity and growth.=?It cannot be proved directly that) Tj T*
(geotropism is due to gravity, because it is not possible to remove) Tj T*
(plants from its influence so as to see how they would behave in) Tj T*
(its absence. The effect of gravity may be neutralized, however, by) Tj T*
(arranging a number of sprouting seeds on the vertical disk of a) Tj T*
(clinostat, an instrument fitted with a clockwork movement by means of) Tj T*
(which they may be kept revolving steadily for several days. By this) Tj T*
(constant change of position gravity is made to act on them in all) Tj T*
(directions alike, which is the same in some respects as if it did not) Tj T*
(act at all. If the disk is made to revolve rapidly, the growing root) Tj T*
(tips turn toward the axis of motion, without showing a tendency to) Tj T*
(grow downward. We may then conclude that geotropism is a reaction to) Tj T*
(gravity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=53. Geotropism an active force.=?It must be noted, however, that the) Tj T*
(force here alluded to is not the mere mechanical effect of gravity,) Tj T*
(due to weight of parts, as when the bough of a fruit tree is bent) Tj T*
(under the load of its crop, but a certain stimulus to which the plant) Tj T*
(reacts by a spontaneous adjustment of its growing parts. In other) Tj T*
(words, geotropism is an active, not a passive function, and the plant) Tj T*
(will overcome considerable resistance in response to it. \(Exp. 38\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=54. Other factors.=?The direction of growth is influenced by many) Tj T*
(other factors, such as light, heat, moisture, contact with other) Tj T*
(bodies, and perhaps by electricity. The result of all these forces is) Tj T*
(an endless variety in the forms and growth of organs that seems to) Tj T*
(defy all law.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
