(laid horizontally, righting itself through the influence of negative) Tj T*
(geotropism.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Heat, unless excessive, generally stimulates growth; contact) Tj T*
(sometimes stimulates it, causing the stem to curve away from the) Tj T*
(disturbing object, and sometimes retards it, causing the stem to) Tj T*
(curve toward the object of contact by growing more rapidly on the) Tj T*
(opposite side, as in the stems of twining vines. Light stimulates) Tj T*
(nutrition, but generally retards growth. The movements of plants) Tj T*
(toward the light are effected in this way; growth being checked on) Tj T*
(that side, the plant bends toward the light.) Tj T*
