(This mode of branching from the central axis instead of from the) Tj T*
(external layers, as in the stem, is one marked distinction between) Tj T*
(the structure of the two organs. In stems, moreover, branches occur) Tj T*
(normally above the points of leaf insertion at the nodes \(46\), while) Tj T*
(in the root they tend to arrange themselves in straight vertical) Tj T*
(rows. The shoots and cions that often originate from them are not) Tj T*
(normal root branches, but outgrowths from irregular or _adventitious_) Tj T*
(buds, that may occur on any part of a plant. The root is not divided) Tj T*
(into nodes like the stem, and never bears leaves.) Tj T*
