(=66. The active part of the root.=?It is only the newest and most) Tj T*
(delicate parts of the root that produce hairs and are engaged in the) Tj T*
(active work of absorption, the older parts acting mainly as carriers.) Tj T*
(Hence, old roots lose much of their characteristic structure and) Tj T*
(take on more and more of the office of the stem, until there is) Tj T*
(practically no difference between them. On the sides of gullies,) Tj T*
(where the earth has been washed from around the trees, we often) Tj T*
(see the upper portion of the root covered with a thick bark and) Tj T*
(fulfilling every office of a true stem.) Tj T*
