(          Field Work) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  \(1\) Examine the underground parts of hardy winter herbs in your) Tj T*
(  neighborhood, also of any weeds or grasses that are particularly) Tj T*
(  troublesome, and see if there is anything about the structure of) Tj T*
(  these parts to account for their persistence. Note the difference) Tj T*
(  between roots of the same species in low, moist places and in) Tj T*
(  dry ones; between those of the same kind of plants in different) Tj T*
(  soils; in sheltered and in exposed situations. Study the direction) Tj T*
(  and position of the roots of trees and shrubs with reference to) Tj T*
(  any stream or body of water in the neighborhood. \(The elm, fig,) Tj T*
(  mulberry, and willow are good subjects for such observations.\)) Tj T*
(  Notice also whether there is any relation between the underground) Tj T*
(  parts and the leaf systems of plants in reference to drainage and) Tj T*
(  transpiration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  \(2\) Observe the effect of root pull upon low herbs. Look along) Tj T*
(  washes and gullies for roots doing the office of stems, and note) Tj T*
(  any changes of structure consequent thereon. Study the relative) Tj T*
(  length and strength of the root systems of different plants, with) Tj T*
(  reference to their value as soil binders, or their hurtfulness in) Tj T*
(  damaging the walls of cellars, wells, sewers, etc. Dig your trowel) Tj T*
(  a few inches into the soil of any grove or copse you happen to) Tj T*
(  visit, note the inextricable tangle of roots, and consider the) Tj T*
(  fierce competition for living room in the vegetable world that it) Tj T*
(  implies.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  \(3\) Tests might be made of the different soils in the neighborhood) Tj T*
(  of the schoolhouse by planting seeds of various kinds and noting) Tj T*
(  the rate of germination; first, without fertilizers, then by adding) Tj T*
(  the different elements in succession to see what is lacking. The) Tj T*
(  field for study suggested by this subject is almost inexhaustible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
