(Birds which destroy insects should be protected; sheep and hogs) Tj T*
(should be kept out, and dead leaves left on the ground to cover the) Tj T*
(roots and fertilize the soil with the humus created by their decay.) Tj T*
(Finally, none but mature trees should be cut for industrial purposes,) Tj T*
(and the cutting ought to be done in such a way that the young) Tj T*
(surrounding growth will not be injured by the falling trunks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=142. The usefulness of forests.=?Aside from the value of their) Tj T*
(products, forests are useful in many other ways. They influence) Tj T*
(climate beneficially by acting as windbreaks, by giving off moisture) Tj T*
(\(Exp. 58\), by shading the soil, and thus preventing too rapid) Tj T*
(evaporation. Their roots also help to retain the water in the soil,) Tj T*
(and by this means tend to prevent the washing of the land by heavy) Tj T*
(rains and to restrain the violence of freshets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=143. Forests and water supply.=?It is especially important that) Tj T*
(the watershed of any region should be well protected by forests,) Tj T*
(to prevent contamination of the streams and to insure an unfailing) Tj T*
(supply of water by checking the escape of the rainfall from the soil.) Tj T*
