(=155. Folding of the leaves.=?Remove the scales from a bud of) Tj T*
(horse-chestnut nearly ready to open, and notice the manner in) Tj T*
(which the young leaves are folded. This is called _vernation_, or) Tj T*
(_prefoliation_, words meaning respectively ?spring condition? and) Tj T*
(?condition preceding the leaf.? Leaves are packed in the bud so as to) Tj T*
(occupy the least space possible, and in different plants they will be) Tj T*
(found folded in a great many different ways, according to the shape) Tj T*
(and texture of the leaf and the space available for it in the bud.) Tj T*
(When doubled back and forth like a fan, or crumpled and folded as in) Tj T*
(the buckeye, horse-chestnut, and maple, the vernation is _plicate_) Tj T*
(\(Figs. 160, 162\).) Tj T*
