(=182. Distribution of stomata.=?While stomata are generally more) Tj T*
(abundant on the under side of leaves, this is not always the case.) Tj T*
(In vertical leaves, like those of the iris, which have both sides) Tj T*
(equally exposed to the sun, they are distributed equally on both) Tj T*
(sides. In plants like the water lily, where the under surface lies) Tj T*
(upon the water, they occur only on the upper side. Succulent leaves,) Tj T*
(as a general thing, have very few, because they need to conserve all) Tj T*
(their moisture. Submerged leaves have none at all; why?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 220.?A small piece of the under epidermis of) Tj T*
(an oak leaf, highly magnified to show the stomata, _g_, and minute) Tj T*
(hairs, _h_.]) Tj T*
