(heat. An interesting example of this kind of adjustment is furnished) Tj T*
(by the rosinweed, or compass plant \(_Silphium laciniatum_, Figs. 238,) Tj T*
(239\), which grows in the prairies of Alabama and westward, where it) Tj T*
(is exposed to intense sunlight. The leaves not only stand vertical,) Tj T*
(but have a tendency to turn their edges north and south so that the) Tj T*
(blades are exposed only to the gentler morning and evening rays. The) Tj T*
