(=242. Significance of these distinctions.=?These distinctions are) Tj T*
(important to remember, not only because they are very useful in) Tj T*
(grouping and classifying plants, but because they mark successive) Tj T*
(stages in the evolution of the flower. In general, flowers of a) Tj T*
(primitive type and less advanced organization are characterized) Tj T*
(by having their organs free and hypogynous, while the more highly) Tj T*
(developed forms show a tendency to consolidation and union of parts,) Tj T*
(and the epigynous mode of insertion. Irregularity also, since it) Tj T*
(indicates specialization and adaptation to a particular purpose, may) Tj T*
(be regarded as a mark of advanced evolution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIGS. 325, 326.?Salvia: 325, longitudinal section) Tj T*
(through a flower, showing the rocking connective which is struck at) Tj T*
(_a_ by a visiting insect; 326, section of the same flower after being) Tj T*
(visited, showing the lower arm of the connective pushed back and) Tj T*
(lowering the anther.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
