(about the wonderful modifications that these organs are capable of) Tj T*
(undergoing; and finally, an examination of a number of different) Tj T*
(flowers has shown them capable of undergoing modifications to an) Tj T*
(equal or even greater extent, and examples of the transition of) Tj T*
(almost any floral organ into another may be observed by one who will) Tj T*
(take the trouble to look for it. Stamens and petals are found in all) Tj T*
(stages of transformation, from the slightly flattened filament of) Tj T*
(the star-of-Bethlehem, or the yellow pollen speck on the petal of) Tj T*
(a rose, to the brilliant staminodia, or transformed stamens of the) Tj T*
(canna \(Fig. 327\), which simulate petals so perfectly that their real) Tj T*
(nature is never suspected by the ordinary observer. The transition) Tj T*
(from spines and bracts to the brilliant corolla of the cactus \(Fig.) Tj T*
(328\) is so gradual that we are hardly aware of it till we examine a) Tj T*
(specimen and see it actually going on before our eyes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It must not be supposed, however, that an organ is ever developed as) Tj T*
(one thing and then deliberately changed into something else. When we) Tj T*
(speak loosely of one organ being modified into another, the meaning) Tj T*
(is merely that it has developed into one thing instead of into) Tj T*
(something else that it was equally capable of developing into.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=245. The course of floral evolution.=?For the reasons mentioned,) Tj T*
(the flower is regarded as merely a branch with modified leaves and) Tj T*
(the internodes indefinitely shortened so as to bring the successive) Tj T*
(cycles into close contact, the whole being greatly altered and) Tj T*
(specialized to serve a particular purpose. With this conception) Tj T*
(of the nature of the flower, we can readily see that the less) Tj T*
(specialized its organs are and the more nearly they approach in) Tj T*
(structure and arrangement to the condition of an undifferentiated) Tj T*
(branch, the more primitive and undeveloped is the type to which it) Tj T*
(belongs. On the other hand, if the parts are highly specialized and) Tj T*
(widely differentiated from the crude branch, a proportionately high) Tj T*
(stage of floral evolution is indicated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(          V. FUNCTION AND WORK OF THE FLOWER) Tj T*
