(ovary, on the cob. The time required for the tube to penetrate to the) Tj T*
(ovary varies in different flowers according to the distance traversed) Tj T*
(and the rate of growth. In the crocus it takes from one to three) Tj T*
(days; in the spotted calla, about five days; and in orchids, from ten) Tj T*
(to thirty days. As a rule, it occupies only a few hours. Sometimes) Tj T*
(the pistil is hollow, affording a free passage to the pollen tube;) Tj T*
(in other cases, it is solid, and the growing tube eats its way down,) Tj T*
(as it were, feeding on the substance of the pistil as it grows. How) Tj T*
(is it in the flower you are examining? It takes a grain of pollen) Tj T*
