(outer integument or testa; _q_, inner integument; _t_, cavity of the) Tj T*
(embryo sac; _u_, its basal portion; _z_, oösphere.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=251. Fertilization.=?When a pollen tube has penetrated to the ovary,) Tj T*
(it next enters one of the ovules, usually through the micropyle) Tj T*
(\(Fig. 330, _m_\). There it penetrates the wall of a baglike inclosure) Tj T*
(called the _embryo sac_ \(Fig. 330, _u_, _t_, _z_\), where one of the) Tj T*
(generative cells emitted by the pollen tube fuses with a large cell) Tj T*
(contained in the embryo sac, known as the _germ cell_, or _egg cell_) Tj T*
(\(Fig. 330, _z_\). The fusion of these two bodies is what constitutes) Tj T*
(fertilization. The cell formed by their union finally develops into) Tj T*
(the embryo, and the other contents of the sac into the endosperm, and) Tj T*
(the ripened ovules become seeds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=252. Stability of the process of fertilization.=?The phenomena) Tj T*
(that characterize the functions of fertilization and reproduction) Tj T*
(are the most uniform and stable of all the life processes, varying) Tj T*
(little not only in different species and orders, but throughout the) Tj T*
(whole vegetable kingdom. And since these functions furnish a more) Tj T*
(reliable standard for judging of the real affinities of the different) Tj T*
(groups than do mere external resemblances, which are more liable) Tj T*
(to variation and may often be accidental, they have been chosen by) Tj T*
(botanists as the ultimate basis for the classification of plants.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=253. Embryology.=?The study of the developing plantlet, known as) Tj T*
(_embryology_, is a comparatively recent branch of science, and has) Tj T*
(greatly enlarged our knowledge of the life history of both plants and) Tj T*
(animals, by bringing to light resemblances that exist between the) Tj T*
(most widely divergent species in their earlier stages of development) Tj T*
(and thus showing traces of a common origin. It has shown further,) Tj T*
(that every individual plant or animal, in its development from the) Tj T*
