(and \(2\) when the parent species are not too unlike, it accentuates) Tj T*
(the good effects of crossing, and sometimes gives rise to offspring) Tj T*
(greatly surpassing either parent in size and vigor. In regard to) Tj T*
(variability it may act in three ways: \(1\) the hybrid may wholly) Tj T*
(resemble one parent or the other, in which case there is, of course,) Tj T*
(no variation; \(2\) it may resemble one parent more than the other; or) Tj T*
(\(3\) it may show a blending of the characters of the two, as when a) Tj T*
(cross between a red poppy and a white gives rise to a light pink, or) Tj T*
(a mixed red and white variety. In the first two cases, the characters) Tj T*
(of the parent that manifest themselves are said to be _dominant_;) Tj T*
(those which do not, _recessive_.) Tj T*
