(and confirmed by later investigators is, briefly, this: If two) Tj T*
(parents differing in some fixed characteristic be crossed, the) Tj T*
(entire offspring, in the first generation, will be like the parent) Tj T*
(possessing the dominant quality. If all the seed of this generation) Tj T*
(is planted and carefully protected from foreign pollen, its offspring) Tj T*
(composing the second generation from the parents will vary in the) Tj T*
(proportion of ¾ dominants \(_D_, _D?_, line 2 of the diagram\) to ¼) Tj T*
