(=276. The color of flowers=, being an adaptation to changing external) Tj T*
(conditions, is a very unstable quality, and varies greatly within) Tj T*
(the limits of the same species. Even on the same stem, flowers of) Tj T*
(different colors are often found, due, probably, to hybridization.) Tj T*
(Yet, notwithstanding all this apparently random intermingling of) Tj T*
(hues, the range of color for each species is confined, approximately,) Tj T*
(within certain limits. Nobody has ever seen a blue rose or a yellow) Tj T*
(aster; and though the florist?s art is constantly narrowing the) Tj T*
(application of this law, it still remains true that in a state of) Tj T*
(nature, certain colors seem to be associated together in the floral) Tj T*
(art gamut. Yellow is considered the simplest and most primitive color) Tj T*
(in flowers, and blue the latest and most highly evolved. Yellow,) Tj T*
(white, and purple, in the order named, are the commonest flower) Tj T*
(colors in nature; blue, the rarest. Do you see any relation between) Tj T*
(these facts and the color preferences of insects?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
