(          Field Work) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  1. The ecology of the flower is so suggestive a subject and so) Tj T*
(  peculiarly appropriate to outdoor work that it seems hardly) Tj T*
(  necessary to point out the many attractive fields of inquiry it) Tj T*
(  opens to the student of nature. In this way alone can experiments) Tj T*
(  in insect pollination be carried on to the best advantage. Try) Tj T*
(  the effect of enveloping buds of various kinds in gauze so as) Tj T*
(  to exclude the visits of insects, and note the result as to the) Tj T*
(  production of fruit and seed. Envelop a cluster of milkweed) Tj T*
(  blossoms in this way and notice how much longer the flowers so) Tj T*
(  protected continue in bloom than do the others; why is this? Try) Tj T*
(  the same experiment upon the blooms of cotton and hibiscus, if you) Tj T*
(  live where they grow, and see whether the characteristic change in) Tj T*
(  color occurs in flowers from which insects have been excluded, and) Tj T*
(  whether good seed pods are produced by them. Try the effect upon) Tj T*
(  fruit production of excluding insects from clusters of apple, pear,) Tj T*
(  and peach blossoms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  2. Make a list of all the outdoor plants, both wild and cultivated,) Tj T*
(  that are found blooming in your neighborhood, keeping a record of) Tj T*
(  the earliest specimens of each as you find them. The best way is to) Tj T*
(  keep a sort of daily calendar, and at the end of each month give a) Tj T*
(  summary of the species found in bloom during that period. In this) Tj T*
(  way a fairly complete annual record of the flowering time of the) Tj T*
(  different plants for that vicinity will be obtained. The record) Tj T*
(  should be kept up the whole year round. Don?t stop in winter,) Tj T*
(  but go straight on through the coldest as well as the hottest) Tj T*
(  season, and you will make some surprising discoveries, especially) Tj T*
(  if the record is continued year after year. Give the common name) Tj T*
(  of each plant, adding the botanical one if you know it. Any facts) Tj T*
(  that you may know or may discover in regard to particular plants,) Tj T*
(  such as their medicinal or other uses, their poisonous or edible) Tj T*
(  properties, the insects that visit them, and in the case of weeds,) Tj T*
(  their origin and introduction, will greatly enhance the interest) Tj T*
(  and value of the record.) Tj T*
