(=302. Accessory fruits= are so called because some other part than) Tj T*
(the seed vessel, or ovary proper, is coherent with, or accessory to) Tj T*
(it, in forming the fruit, as in the apple and the hip. The accessory) Tj T*
(part may consist of any organ, but is more frequently the calyx or) Tj T*
(the receptacle. In the strawberry, the little hard bodies, usually) Tj T*
(called seeds, that dot the surface are the true fruits \(akenes\). A) Tj T*
(vertical section through the center will show the edible part to) Tj T*
(consist wholly of the enlarged receptacle. In the pineapple, the) Tj T*
(edible stalk may be traced through a mass of flowers whose seed) Tj T*
(vessels have become enlarged and ripened into fruits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=303. Aggregate fruits.=?Some accessory fruits, the strawberry and) Tj T*
(blackberry for example, are, at the same time, aggregate; that is,) Tj T*
(they are composed of a number of separate individual fruits produced) Tj T*
(from a single flower. The cone of the magnolia and of the tulip tree) Tj T*
(are aggregate fruits; can you name any others?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIGS. 402-404.?Multiple fruit of the pineapple: 402,) Tj T*
(external view of a ripe fruit, showing the prolonged receptacle) Tj T*
(growing into a new plant above, and the scaly bracted covering below;) Tj T*
(403, vertical section through the axis of a fruit, showing _a_, the) Tj T*
(receptacle, with _b_, _b_, the fleshy ovaries cohering around it) Tj T*
(and forming the edible part of fruit; 404, a single ?eye? or scale,) Tj T*
(somewhat reduced, showing the scaly bract from the axil of which the) Tj T*
(\(generally\) abortive flower originates.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=304. Collective, or multiple, fruits.=?The pineapple is an example) Tj T*
(of both an accessory and a multiple fruit, being composed of the) Tj T*
(ripened ovaries of a number of separate flowers that have become) Tj T*
(more or less coherent. The osage orange, sweet gum balls, fig, and) Tj T*
(mulberry are other examples of this class.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=305. Dissection of a multiple fruit.=?Get one of the dried figs sold) Tj T*
(by the grocers. Look at the small end where the skin originates; of) Tj T*
(what part is it a modification? \(289.\) Can think of a reason for this) Tj T*
(curious, urnlike enlargement of the receptacle? Is there anything) Tj T*
(about the fig, for instance, that renders it peculiarly liable to be) Tj T*
(preyed upon by birds and insects? Could any but a very small insect) Tj T*
(get through the eye without injuring the fruit? Could it free itself) Tj T*
(from the sticky mass inside and get out again without difficulty?) Tj T*
(Would you judge from this that the caprification of the fig is easily) Tj T*
(effected \(279\), even when the fig wasp is present? Can you now) Tj T*
(account for the fact that over four hundred varieties of cultivated) Tj T*
(figs ripen their fruit without fertilization?) Tj T*
