(the pulp of the fig consists of hundreds of tiny pistillate blossoms) Tj T*
(that line the inner face of the receptacle. The little grains) Tj T*
(usually taken for seeds are really small akenes?the ripened ovaries) Tj T*
(of flowers that have been pollinated from the caprifig \(279, 286\).) Tj T*
