(=306. Fruit clusters.=?Be careful not to confound aggregate and) Tj T*
(collective fruits with mere clusters, like a bunch of grapes or of) Tj T*
(sumac berries. The distinction is not always easy to make out. The) Tj T*
(clump of akenes that make up a dandelion ball, for instance, though) Tj T*
(held on a common receptacle, like the mulberry and other collective) Tj T*
(fruits, have so little connection with each other, and separate) Tj T*
(so completely at maturity, as to partake more of the nature of a) Tj T*
(cluster than of a collective fruit. The same is true of the clump) Tj T*
(of tailed akenes that make up the fruit of the clematis. Though the) Tj T*
(product of a single flower and thus technically an aggregate fruit,) Tj T*
(they are really only a compact head or cluster. Some degree of) Tj T*
(cohesion is necessary to constitute a cluster of matured ovaries into) Tj T*
(an aggregate or a multiple fruit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=307. The individual fruits= that make up the various kinds just) Tj T*
