(=316. Modes of grouping.=?Plants group themselves in their favorite) Tj T*
(habitats, not according to their botanical relationships, but with) Tj T*
(regard to the predominance of one or more of the ecological factors) Tj T*
(that influence their growth. Sometimes one or two species will) Tj T*
(take practical possession of large areas, like the coarse grasses) Tj T*
(that spread over certain salt marshes, or the pines that formerly) Tj T*
(constituted the sole forest growth over extensive regions in North) Tj T*
(Carolina and Maine. Exclusive growths of this kind over limited) Tj T*
(areas are sometimes called plant _colonies_, and the individuals) Tj T*
(composing them belong, as a general thing, to the hardy, pushing sort) Tj T*
(known as ?pioneers,? which are among the first to take possession) Tj T*
