(Any well-defined assemblage of plants, whether of one kind or many,) Tj T*
(originating in such a common response to the same influences, is) Tj T*
(called a _formation_. These associations are variously classed,) Tj T*
(according to the nature of their habitat, as salt water, fresh water,) Tj T*
(sand hill, swamp, bog, river bottom, or such other kinds as their) Tj T*
(ecological character may indicate. Local conditions in limited) Tj T*
(areas may lead to the segregation of smaller and more compact groups) Tj T*
(called _societies_. This term, however, is used rather loosely, being) Tj T*
(treated in some works as synonymous with formations, in others as) Tj T*
(analogous with what have here been defined as colonies.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
