(=329. Climatic zones.=?These are more general groupings than those) Tj T*
(we have been considering. They follow in a rough way the parallels) Tj T*
(of latitude, and are classed accordingly as: \(1\) tropical; \(2\)) Tj T*
(subtropical; \(3\) temperate; \(4\) boreal or \(on mountains\) subalpine;) Tj T*
(\(5\) arctic or \(on high mountains\) alpine. Taking the cultivated) Tj T*
(plants of our own country by way of illustration, we have the) Tj T*
(subtropical zone, embracing Florida and the southern portion of the) Tj T*
(Gulf states, where sugar cane, rice, and tropical fruits are the) Tj T*
(staple crops. Then comes the temperate zone, with three agricultural) Tj T*
(subdivisions: \(_a_\) the great cotton belt, with Indian corn, sweet) Tj T*
(potatoes, and the peach, melon, and fig as secondary products.) Tj T*
(Farther north, in the Central and Middle Atlantic states, we find) Tj T*
(\(_b_\) the region of maize, hemp, and tobacco, with grapes, apples,) Tj T*
(pears, cherries, and a great variety of garden vegetables as side) Tj T*
(crops. Finally comes \(_c_\) the great wheat-growing region of the) Tj T*
(North, with buckwheat, hay, and Irish potatoes as subsidiary crops.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Technically, the distribution of the natural zones of vegetation from) Tj T*
(south to north is classed under the three general heads of Forest,) Tj T*
(Grass Land, and Arctic Desert, with numerous subdivisions in each.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=330. Boundaries of the zones.=?While the broad continental zones) Tj T*
(of vegetation follow, in a general way, the climatic zones outlined) Tj T*
(above, they are not sharply defined, but run into each other and) Tj T*
(overlap in various degrees, so that a map depicting the range of) Tj T*
(vegetation in any wide area would show a marked deviation from those) Tj T*
(of latitude. Various other geographical factors, such as mountain) Tj T*
(ranges and bodies of water, influence the direction and character of) Tj T*
(the prevailing winds and rains, and through them the moisture and) Tj T*
(temperature, to so great an extent that they become the controlling) Tj T*
(factors over wide areas. In countries bordering on the sea, the coast) Tj T*
(line always marks a belt of its own, and on the sides of a mountain) Tj T*
(range, all the climatic zones from the equator to the pole may be) Tj T*
(repeated during an ascent of a few miles.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In our own country, where the mountain chains and coast lines run) Tj T*
(approximately north and south, the great continental zones have been) Tj T*
(superseded, for all practical purposes, by four regional divisions) Tj T*
(running almost at right angles to them. These are, disregarding minor) Tj T*
(subdivisions:?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\) The Forest region, occupying the eastern and south central) Tj T*
(portion of the Union. In classifying this territory as forest, it is) Tj T*
(not meant to imply that it is now, or ever was, one unbroken jungle,) Tj T*
(like parts of central Africa, but that it combines the conditions) Tj T*
