(=335. III. Pteridophytes=, or fern plants, are classed roughly in) Tj T*
(the three divisions of ferns, horsetails, and club mosses. They) Tj T*
(differ greatly in structure, but all possess a vascular system, and) Tj T*
(a well-organized structure of root, stem, and leaves. They rank next) Tj T*
(to the spermatophytes in the order of development, and the group is) Tj T*
(of especial interest on account of its relationship to the higher) Tj T*
(plants. One of its divisions, the club mosses, has probably given) Tj T*
(rise to at least one section of the gymnosperms, while the ferns are) Tj T*
(regarded as the ancestors of the true flowering plants, which make) Tj T*
(up the great class of angiosperms, and represent the highest type of) Tj T*
(evolution yet attained in the vegetable kingdom.) Tj T*
