(=336. Variety of forms.=?This group embraces plants of the greatest) Tj T*
(diversity of form and structure, from the minute volvox and desmids) Tj T*
(that hover near the uncertain boundaries dividing the vegetable from) Tj T*
(the animal world, to the giant kelps of the ocean, which sometimes) Tj T*
(attain a length of from six hundred to one thousand feet. They are) Tj T*
(usually classed according to their color, as green, brown, and red) Tj T*
(algæ, including various subdivisions of each group. They all contain) Tj T*
(chlorophyll, by means of which they manufacture their own food,) Tj T*
(though in the red and brown divisions it is masked by the presence of) Tj T*
(other pigments?an adaptation to the modified light that reaches them) Tj T*
(at various depths under water. With few exceptions they can live only) Tj T*
(in the water, and unlike any other form of plant life, attain their) Tj T*
(highest development in the salty depths of the ocean. The freshwater) Tj T*
(forms are small and inconspicuous, and generally of a more simple) Tj T*
(type than the seaweeds. The great majority of them belong to the two) Tj T*
(classes of green and blue-green algæ. The former is believed to have) Tj T*
(furnished the type from which the higher plants have been evolved.) Tj T*
