(\(369\). These plants are all, with a few doubtful exceptions,) Tj T*
(parasites or saprophytes which contain no chlorophyll and are) Tj T*
(incapable of supporting an independent existence. Biologists are) Tj T*
(divided as to their position in the genealogical tree of life.) Tj T*
(The weight of authority at present inclines to the view that they) Tj T*
(are degenerate forms derived from the algæ, but they have been so) Tj T*
(modified by their parasitic habits as to render their position in the) Tj T*
(general scheme of life a doubtful one. They represent an offshoot,) Tj T*
