(=346. Useful fungi.=?Not all fungi, however, are injurious. On the) Tj T*
(contrary, the great majority of them are harmless, and very many) Tj T*
(kinds are positively beneficial to man. Without the yeasts and) Tj T*
(bacteria of fermentation we could not have our bread and cheese.) Tj T*
(Other forms are active agents in the fertilization of soils, it) Tj T*
(having been estimated that there are 100,000 or more of these) Tj T*
(infinitesimal laborers at work in every cubic centimeter \(about ¹???) Tj T*
(of a cubic inch\) of virgin soil! Even the bacteria of putrefaction,) Tj T*
(which we are accustomed to regard as the embodiment of all that is) Tj T*
(foul and loathesome, are engaged in an unceasing work as scavengers,) Tj T*
(without which life would no longer be possible on our globe, as will) Tj T*
(be shown in the following section.) Tj T*
