(It was formerly supposed that black rust was caused by a different) Tj T*
(fungus from that producing red rust, and to it the name _Puccinia_) Tj T*
(was given. This has been retained as a general designation for all) Tj T*
(fungi undergoing these two phases, and the particular form of fungus) Tj T*
(that we are now considering is known in all its stages as _Puccinia) Tj T*
(graminis_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=361. The nonparasitic stage.=?The formation of teleutospores) Tj T*
(completes that portion of the life history of the fungus during which) Tj T*
(it is parasitic on wheat and grasses of different kinds. In spring) Tj T*
(they begin to germinate on the ground, each cell producing a small) Tj T*
(filament, from which arise in turn several small branches. Upon the) Tj T*
(tip of each of these branches is developed a tiny sporelike body) Tj T*
(called a _sporidium_ \(Fig. 454\), which continues the generation of) Tj T*
(the rust fungus through the next stage of its existence. The filament) Tj T*
(which bears these sporidia is not parasitic, but when the sporidia) Tj T*
(ripen and the spores contained in them are scattered by the wind,) Tj T*
(there begins a second parasitic phase, which forms the most curious) Tj T*
(part of this strange life history.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=362. The æcidium.=?Examine next the under side of some barberry) Tj T*
(leaves \(or comfrey, etc., if orange leaf-rust is used\) for clusters) Tj T*
(of small whitish bodies that appear under the lens like little white) Tj T*
(corollas with yellow anthers in the center. Examine a section of one) Tj T*
(of these under the microscope and notice that the yellow substance) Tj T*
(is composed of regular layers of colored spores. The corolla-like) Tj T*
(receptacles containing them, popularly known as ?cluster cups,?) Tj T*
(are borne on a mycelium produced from the spores described in the) Tj T*
(last paragraph. This mycelium is parasitic on barberry or other) Tj T*
(leaves, according to the kind of fungus, and was long believed to be) Tj T*
(a distinct plant, to which the name _Æcidium_ \(pl., _Æcidia_\) was) Tj T*
(given. This term is now applied to the cluster cups, and those fungi) Tj T*
(which at any period of their life history produce them are called) Tj T*
(æcidium fungi.) Tj T*
ET
