(=363. Spermogonia.=?On the upper surface of the leaves that bear) Tj T*
(the æcidia, notice some small black dots hardly larger than pin) Tj T*
(points, but which, when sufficiently magnified, appear as little) Tj T*
(flask-shaped bodies \(Fig. 455\) under the epidermis. These are known) Tj T*
(as _spermogonia_, or _pycnidia_. When mature, they break through) Tj T*
(the epidermis so that the necks protrude, and discharge a quantity) Tj T*
(of minute cells or spores, very like some that, later on, we shall) Tj T*
(find playing an important part in the reproductive processes of) Tj T*
(certain other fungi, and of mosses and liverworts. In the rust fungi,) Tj T*
(however, their function is not understood. They may possibly be) Tj T*
(survivals of organs which were once active in the life processes of) Tj T*
(the plant, but have become useless under changed conditions. Do such) Tj T*
(organs throw any light on the evolutionary history of plants?) Tj T*
