(=367. Mushrooms and toadstools.=?The popular distinction which limits) Tj T*
(the term ?mushroom? to a single species, the _Agaricus campestris_,) Tj T*
(and classes all others as toadstools, has no sanction in botany. All) Tj T*
(mushrooms are toadstools and all toadstools are mushrooms, whether) Tj T*
(poisonous or edible. The real distinction is between mushrooms and) Tj T*
(puffballs, the former term being more properly applied to fungi which) Tj T*
(have the spore-bearing surface exposed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=368. Examination of a typical specimen.=?The most highly specialized) Tj T*
(of the fungi, and the easiest to observe on account of their size and) Tj T*
(abundance, are the mushrooms that are such familiar objects after) Tj T*
(every summer shower. The _gilled_ kind?those with the rayed laminæ) Tj T*
(under the cap?are usually the most easily obtained. Specimens should) Tj T*
(be examined as soon after gathering as possible, since they decay) Tj T*
(very quickly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=369. The mycelium.=?Examine some of the white fibrous substance) Tj T*
(usually called spawn through a lens. Notice that it is made up of) Tj T*
(fine white threads interlacing with each other, and often forming) Tj T*
(webby mats that ramify to a considerable distance through the) Tj T*
(substratum of rotten wood or other material upon which the fungus) Tj T*
(grows. This webby structure, often mistaken for root fibers, is) Tj T*
(the thallus or true vegetative body of the plant, the part rising) Tj T*
(above ground, and usually regarded as the mushroom, being only the) Tj T*
(fruit, or reproductive organ. Place some of the mycelium under the) Tj T*
(microscope and notice that it is composed of delicate filaments made) Tj T*
(up of single cells placed end to end, as in Spirogyra \(341\). These) Tj T*
(filaments are called _hyphæ_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=370. The button.=?Look on the mycelium for one of the small round) Tj T*
(bodies called buttons \(Fig. 457\). These are the beginning of the) Tj T*
(fruiting body popularly known as the mushroom, and are of various) Tj T*
(sizes, some of the youngest being barely visible to the naked eye.) Tj T*
(After a time they begin to elongate and make their way out of the) Tj T*
(substratum.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
