(=418. Retrogressive evolution.=?While the general course of evolution) Tj T*
(has been upward and onward, the movement has not always followed) Tj T*
(a straight line, but, like a mountain road, shows many windings) Tj T*
(and deviations from the direct route. The monocotyls furnish a) Tj T*
(conspicuous example of this departure from the general law of) Tj T*
(progression. It was formerly supposed, on account of their greater) Tj T*
