(We should remember, too, that while progressive evolution implies) Tj T*
(successful adjustment to surroundings, it is possible to conceive of) Tj T*
(a state, as our planet approaches the period of cosmic debility and) Tj T*
(decay, when the conditions of existence may become progressively more) Tj T*
(and more unfavorable. In this case the course of evolution would be) Tj T*
(reversed, the higher types gradually dying out as the struggle for) Tj T*
(life became more severe, and the tendency would be constantly toward) Tj T*
(lower and simpler forms, until finally all life would become extinct) Tj T*
(on our planet. We have no right, however, to assume that during such) Tj T*
(a course of retrogressive evolution the same forms would be repeated) Tj T*
(in reverse order as have already appeared, because there is no reason) Tj T*
(to believe that the conditions brought about by planetary decline and) Tj T*
(?old age? would be the same as those attending planetary birth and) Tj T*
(adolescence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 511.?Diagram showing the supposed course of plant) Tj T*
(evolution.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=419. Explanation of the diagram.=?An attempt to show the general) Tj T*
(course of plant evolution up to the present time is made in the) Tj T*
(accompanying diagram. The four great divisions, Thallophytes,) Tj T*
(Bryophytes, Pteridophytes, and Spermatophytes, are represented by) Tj T*
(spaces between four horizontal lines arranged one above the other in) Tj T*
(the order of their succession in time and complexity of organization.) Tj T*
(It should be borne in mind that these dividing lines are not sharply) Tj T*
(defined in nature, but overlap or indent the territory between them) Tj T*
(with varying degrees of irregularity, like the coast line on a) Tj T*
(map. The relative positions of the different orders we have been) Tj T*
(considering are represented by upright and diagonal lines, the) Tj T*
(general course of which, as indicated by the arrows, is intended to) Tj T*
(give an idea of the trend of evolutionary progress in the particular) Tj T*
(group represented by each line. No one of these lines is made to) Tj T*
(originate directly in any other, because, with the possible exception) Tj T*
(of the monocotyls, we have no authority for asserting that any such) Tj T*
(direct connection exists between plants as we know them, but only) Tj T*
(that certain types give evidence of descent from a common ancestry.) Tj T*
(This lack of certainty is expressed by placing the point of origin) Tj T*
(for any given line in more or less close proximity to the one which) Tj T*
(is supposed to be the nearest living representative of the common) Tj T*
(ancestor. The line of ferns, for instance, is depicted as originating) Tj T*
(in the region of the bryophytes, somewhere in the neighborhood of) Tj T*
(the liverworts, but the two lines nowhere come in contact, because) Tj T*
(there is no evidence that any fern, living or fossil, is directly) Tj T*
(descended from any particular kind of liverwort known to us. With) Tj T*
(these explanations, the diagram shows, in a rough way, the generally) Tj T*
(accepted view of plant relationships as based on the evidence at) Tj T*
(present before us. But in questions of this sort it is wise to keep) Tj T*
(in mind the blunt remark of a famous old American statesman, that) Tj T*
(?only fools and dead people never change their opinions.?) Tj T*
ET
endstream
