(  in the woods and those in open ground. Find out how those on the) Tj T*
(  ground get their nourishment. Uncover the mycelium, and notice) Tj T*
(  the extent of its surface. Examine the soil and find out if it) Tj T*
(  contains anything upon which they could feed. Note the prevalence) Tj T*
(  of shelf fungi on trees. Examine the condition of the wood where) Tj T*
(  they grow, and decide in what ways they injure their hosts. Notice) Tj T*
(  whether they abound most on healthy or on decaying trunks and) Tj T*
(  boughs, and decide whether this is because the fungus prefers that) Tj T*
(  kind of host, or whether the injury it does causes the decay, or) Tj T*
(  whether both causes operate together. Notice what fungi grow on) Tj T*
(  different trees, and study their preferences in this respect.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  3. Observe the different kinds of lichens found in your walks) Tj T*
(  and try to distinguish the three classes. Which kind are most) Tj T*
