() Tj T*
(=Principles of classification.=?All the known plants in the world,) Tj T*
(numbering not less than one hundred and twenty thousand species) Tj T*
(of the seed-bearing kind alone, are ranged according to certain) Tj T*
(resemblances of structure, into a number of great groups known as) Tj T*
(families or orders. The names of these families are distinguished by) Tj T*
(the ending _aceæ_; the rose family, for instance, are the _Rosaceæ_;) Tj T*
(the pink family, _Caryophyllaceæ_; the walnut family, _Juglandaceæ_,) Tj T*
(etc. Each of these families is divided into lesser groups called) Tj T*
(_genera_ \(singular, _genus_\), characterized by similarities showing) Tj T*
(a still greater degree of affinity than that which marks the larger) Tj T*
(groups or orders; and finally, when the differences between the) Tj T*
(individual plants of a kind are so small as to be disregarded, they) Tj T*
(are considered to form one species; all the common morning-glories,) Tj T*
(for instance, of whatever shade or color, belong to the species) Tj T*
(_Ipomea purpurea_. The small differences that arise within a species) Tj T*
(as to the color and size of flowers, and other minor points,) Tj T*
(constitute mere varieties, and have no special names applied to them.) Tj T*
(The line between varieties and species is not clearly defined, and) Tj T*
(in the nature of things can never be, since progressive development,) Tj T*
(through unceasing change, is the law of all life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In botanical descriptions, the name both of the species and the genus) Tj T*
(is given, just as in designating a person, like Mary Jones or John) Tj T*
(Robinson, we give both the surname and the Christian name. The genus,) Tj T*
(or generic name, answers to the surname, and that of the species to) Tj T*
(the Christian name?except that in botanical nomenclature the order) Tj T*
(is reversed, the generic, or surname, coming first, and the specific) Tj T*
(or individual name last; for example, _Ipomea_ is the generic, or) Tj T*
(surname, of the morning-glories, and _purpurea_ the specific one.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=How to use the key.=?Any good manual will answer the purpose. Gray?s) Tj T*
(?School and Field Book? is, perhaps, the best available at present) Tj T*
(for the states east of the Mississippi. Reference to the floral) Tj T*
(analyses in sections =I-IV= of Chapter VII will make its use clear.) Tj T*
