(=Making collections.=?Mere labeled aggregations of species are not) Tj T*
(recommended, but the collection of examples illustrating special) Tj T*
(points in morphology and plant variation may be made with profit;) Tj T*
(such, for instance, as the adaptations observed in tendrils and) Tj T*
(stipular appendages, the various modifications of leaves and stems) Tj T*
(to serve other than their normal purposes, or the different forms) Tj T*
(of leaves and flowers on the same stem, or on different plants of) Tj T*
(the same species. A collection made with some specific object in) Tj T*
(view would also be instructive, and might prove of great value; for) Tj T*
(instance, to get together examples of all the troublesome weeds of) Tj T*
(a locality for the purpose of studying their habits and devising) Tj T*
(means for their eradication; or of all the native useful plants, with) Tj T*
(detailed analyses of their economic properties, and observations on) Tj T*
(their habits and the practicability of further developing them. In) Tj T*
(short, wherever collecting is carried on, it should be done with some) Tj T*
(object other than the mere identification of species, which often) Tj T*
(results in greater detriment to the wild plants of a neighborhood) Tj T*
(than profit to the collector.) Tj T*
